<h2 id="a-problem-encountered-in-development">A Problem Encountered in Development</h2>

<p>How to correctly use a block’s <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">weakSelf</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">strongSelf</code> across multiple nested blocks in Objective-C.</p>

<p>In Objective-C, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">weak self</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">strong self</code> are used to break retain cycles. When you use <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">self</code> as a parameter of a block, you need to use <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">__weak typeof(self) weakSelf = self;</code> to create a weak reference in order to avoid a retain cycle. Then, inside the block, you can use <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">strongSelf</code> to obtain a strong reference.</p>

